From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:32:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] smp: check that DRAM was kept before a T8132 S2R wake
 resumes the OS

Two J604 (T8132) deep sleeps reset about 78 s after the wake: inside
the resume stub's 60 s window, before the OS's next mark. Whether DRAM
was kept through the sleep is the first thing to settle there, and only
aura runs on the wake path before the OS touches its saved state.

Let the OS have aura check it. The mailbox grows from 32 to 112 bytes,
and /chosen/aurora,s2r-mailbox-size says so, so an OS writes the new
fields only into a mailbox that has them. Before its commit the OS names
up to four ranges (by physical address, 64 KiB each, 256 KiB in all,
cleaned to PoC), their CRC-32 (zlib's, one stream over the ranges in
order) and, last, check_magic "AURACRC1". Before taking resume_pa, aura
recomputes the CRC with the MMU off, so it reads DRAM itself, and clears
check_magic. A match resumes as before, with WD2 at 40 s. A mismatch
stops with WD2 at 20 s, and ranges outside those limits stop it at 30 s,
so the reset says which. Without check_magic (an older OS) nothing
changes. The magic stays "AURAS2R1", so an older OS finds the mailbox as
before. T8132 only.

Assisted-by: LLM
